Subject: [PATCH 102/230] Give the Matchday feed one header style, a denser
 card and a calmer top
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The feed mixed two section-header treatments (plain h2 for My teams, a
disclosure for Live/Upcoming/Previous), and the loading state swapped the
Upcoming heading for a different one once data arrived, so the page visibly
snapped mid-load. My teams is now a CollapsibleSection like its neighbours,
and the loading state uses the same section id, so the header and its stored
open/closed choice survive the swap.

The referral banner sat above the live scores, competing with the page's
"the live moment leads" rule; it moves to the foot of the feed. The selected
league chip now reads as a filled volt pill instead of a border-only
outline, matching the affordance the picker button next to it already used.
Match cards lose a little padding and footer space to fit more fixtures on
the screen without crowding the scoreline.

